      <text bytes="776" sha1="5rvzt7rwooy0i43aain9w85yvudtxje" xml:space="preserve">[[Category:Content]]
Hello, after experimenting with chat Gpt 4 here is the translitiration of the liber primus using number 35,597,295,815,700,145,277 as the factorized mapping for prime numbers in the original Gematria. Results are indeed close to pitch perfect but some places still need some context and logic to have full English sense. My speculation that after "know this" there is two mirrored ciphers present. This theory is based on using AI as decipher mechanism and when AI can decipher known zones it enters into some abstract zone where atbash and xor start to give weird results as transcribing text or turn it upside down. My assumption is that there is 2 simple layers of cipher that can be uncovered.


[https://pastebin.com/J6sXpfRN]
